; Devirtualization with the "sea-dsa" resolver: the candidates come from the
; points-to graph rather than from the signature, so the call in
; test-devirt-sea-dsa.c is promoted to @chosen alone. Running the same input
; through --devirt-functions=types promotes it to @not_chosen as well.
;
; RUN: %clam -O0 --crab-dom=int --devirt-functions=sea-dsa --crab-print-invariants=false --crab-disable-warnings "%s".c -o %t.bc
; RUN: %llvm_dis < %t.bc | OutputCheck %s --comment=";"
; RUN: %llvm_dis < %t.bc | OutputCheck %s --check-prefix=NEG --comment=";"

; The attributes between "define" and the return type vary by host (dso_local
; on Linux, none on macOS), so do not spell them out.
; CHECK: define .*i32 @main
; CHECK: call i32 @chosen\(i32 noundef %call\)

; The store into @fn is the last thing in main that precedes the promoted
; call, and @not_chosen never reaches @fn, so no mention of it may follow.
; NEG: store volatile ptr @chosen, ptr @fn
; NEG-NOT: @not_chosen
